as, Pallanti, S., Cantisani, A., Grassi, G., Antonini, S., Cecchelli, C., Burian, J., et al, Pallanti, Qin, B.-Y., Dai, L.-L., Zheng, Y., Qin, Roose, S. P., Sackeim, H. A., Krishnan, K. R. R., Pollock, B. G., Alexopoulos, G., Lavretsky, H., et al, Roose, Rush, A. J., Trivedi, M. H., Wisniewski, S. R., Nierenberg, A. A., Stewart, J. W., Warden, D., et al, Rush, Salzman, C., Wong, E., Wright, B. C., Salzman, Sanglier, T., Saragoussi, D., Milea, D., Auray, J.-P., Valuck, R. J., Tournier, M., Sanglier, Sanna, A., Fattore, L., Badas, P., Corona, G., Cocco, V., Diana, M., Sanna, Sayar, G. H., Ozten, E., Tan, O., Tarhan, N., Sayar, Sheehan, D. V., Lecrubier, Y., Sheehan, K. H., Amorim, P., Janavs, J., Weiller, E., et al, Sheehan, Sheng, J., Liu, S., Wang, Y., Cui, R., Zhang, X., Sheng, Slotema, C. W., Blom, J. D., Hoek, H. W., Sommer, I. E. C., Slotema, Stahl, S. M., Stahl, S. M., Stahl, Taylor, C. B., Youngblood, M. E., Catellier, D., Veith, R. C., Carney, R. M., Burg, M. M., et al, Taylor, Weaver, K. R., Griffioen, M. A., Klinedinst, N. J., Galik, E., Duarte, A. C., Colloca, L., et al, Weaver, Yarnitsky, D., Yarnitsky, Yary, T., Soleimannejad, K., Abd Rahim, F., Kandiah, M., Aazami, S., Poor, S. J., et al, Yary, Zenebe, Y., Akele, B., Selassie, M., Necho, M., Zenebe
Y1  - 2022//
N2  - Introduction: Transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) is a consolidated procedure for the treatment of depression, with several meta-analyses demonstrating its efficacy. Theta-burst stimulation (TBS) is a modification of TMS with similar efficacy and shorter session duration. The geriatric population has many comorbidities and a high prevalence of depression, but few clinical trials are conducted specifically for this age group. TBS could be an option in this population, offering the advantages of few side effects and no pharmacological interactions. Therefore, our aim is to investigate the efficacy of TBS in geriatric depression. (PsycInfo Database Record (c) 2023 APA, all rights reserved)
